license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository giving skew Hadamard matrices of orders
  4040, 5192, 5960 and 6216 (2^3 times 505, 649, 745 and 777). For each odd
  part, the 2025 table of Cati and Pasechnik records a larger least known
  order; at 505 the recorded power of two drops from 2^11 to 2^3. Each matrix
  comes from four unions of sixteenth-power classes in a prime field
  p = 17 mod 32, placed in the bordered array of Momihara and Xiang. For four
  fixed patterns, a pattern works at a prime (for some primitive root) if and
  only if one ratio of binomial coefficients satisfies a fixed polynomial
  congruence mod p; for three of them, the primes that work are exactly those
  represented by explicit binary quartic forms such as u^4+8u^2v^2+8v^4. All-skew seeds extend to
  skew Hadamard matrices of order 4(p^n+1) for every n. Sequel to "A skew
  Hadamard matrix of order 2120" (doi:10.5281/zenodo.24356140). Novelty is
  bounded to the sources searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - skew Hadamard matrices
  - cyclotomy
  - Jacobi sums
  - binomial coefficients
  - binary quartic forms
